# Testing

## Per layer
- Domain: unit tests for every validator rule and every use case (with mocktail repositories).
- Data: DAOs, repositories and SeedService against an in-memory Drift database from test/helpers/test_database.dart. Network interceptors with a fake HttpClientAdapter.
- Core: Result, failure mapping, MotionPolicy tiers, LayoutMetrics classification, formatters, SyncCoordinator single-flight.
- Config: resolveAuthRedirect for every session and location combination.
- Blocs: bloc_test for loading, data, empty and failure, plus every user event.
- Widgets: each motion primitive including the reduce-motion path, ViewStateBuilder, AppButton loading and double-tap guard, and no overflow at text scale 1.3 across the device matrix.
- Migrations: SchemaVerifier tests for every schema version in test/core/database.
- Integration: integration_test/app_flow_test.dart boots the real app and verifies redirects.

## Naming
- Group by the unit under test. Test names describe behaviour: "emits failure when the repository stream errors", not "test 1".
- One behaviour per test. Arrange, act and assert are visually separated.

## Helpers (test/helpers)
- pumpApp wraps a widget with localization, theme, MotionScope and optional Bloc providers.
- device_matrix.dart runs a test body across the reference sizes at text scale 1.0 and 1.3 and fails on overflow.
- test_database.dart creates an in-memory AppDatabase. fake_clock.dart provides a controllable Clock.
- Register mocktail fallback values in setUpAll when a matcher needs them.

## Rules
- Tests never touch the network, the real secure storage or real time. Inject Clock, delays and platform services.
- Unit and widget tests construct objects directly or use GetIt.asNewInstance() in a helper; they never touch the global getIt.
- A failing test is fixed at the cause, never skipped.
